> Totus, are there any parts of the site I could help to maintain
> without knowledge of Lojban at this stage?

I can only let you know what I do.=A0 For me naintenance means mostly=20
things like checking if the links are still there, restoring them if=20
appropriate, reviewing the English-language text (or other natural=20
language), checking for attachments that may have been planted by=20
outsiders, letting Robin=A0know via the IRC if a page is broken, changing=
=20
appearnace/format to make it look better (e.g. adding a photo) etc.
None of these things require knowledge of Lojban.

For something like the news on the Lojban-language home page,=20
I do my best in Lojban and then ask an experienced Lojbanist to=20
review it before putting it on.=A0 Seems to work.

>=20
